………%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...Ten minutes late.\d%K%P
「…超过１０分钟了」%K%P
It had already been five whole minutes since I last looked\nat the station's clock, which now displayed the time as\n7:10 PM.%K%P
车站前的大钟，从一条直线的状态，过了５分钟，现在是７点１０分。%K%P
It was only ten minutes, but I couldn't help staring at\nthe letters spelling out \dToko\d on my cellphone's screen.%K%P
离约定好的时间只过了１０分钟，\n但我的心情着实焦虑不安，\n盯着三个月前改成了『都子』的液晶画面。%K%P
I had a reason for being so worried about her being late.%K%P
我如此担心她的迟到，是有原因的。%K%P
As to what that reason was... well, you only had to look\nat the sky.%K%P
那个…虽然抬头看看天空就能明白了的就是…%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI'm freezing...!\d%K%P
「好冷！？」%K%P
It seemed like we'd be having a blizzard on our hands\ntonight. The snow had even begun to affect the traffic.%K%P
一个小时之前，突降的雪，\n使得市内的交通有些措手不及，\n这也是今年直到现在，最大的一场雪。%K%P
Thursday, February 14.%K%P
２月１４日，星期四。%K%P
The day heralded as a boon to all confectionery\nmanufacturers nationwide. Otherwise known as Valentine's\nDay.%K%P
今天，是糕点公司针对世间单方面缔结的纪念日。\n名曰『情人节』。。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...Eleven minutes late.\d%K%P
「…超过１１分钟了」%K%P
The station was only a fifteen-minute walk away from the\nTerrace House Hinosaka.%K%P
从Terrace House阳之坂到车站，徒步要走１５分钟。%K%P
But the road had been almost completely covered in snow.%K%P
然而，道路上已经开始积雪起来。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dShe didn't fall or anything, did she? She isn't... hurt\nor anything, right?\d%K%P
「她不会是摔倒了吧？\n没有…受伤吧？」%K%P
I asked Toko out this morning.%K%P
今天早上，我对都子提出了邀约。%K%P
It would be a celebration of her passing those exams. The\ncelebration I postponed due to... my unstable mental\nstate.%K%P
由于我单方面的事情…名为精神状态的原因，\n结果对她升学考试合格的祝贺，整整晚了一个月。%K%P
The plan was to buy her a present, have dinner, walk\naround for a while, and perhaps even get something from\nher in return.%K%P
购买礼物，吃个饭，然后散散步。\n说不定还能从都子那里得到好东西。%K%P
And after we spent a warm evening together, not as a\ncouple, but not quite as family, either...%K%P
似这般，我们既不像是父女，也不像是情侣，\n度过最后的，微妙而和缓的时光。%K%P
...I would give her my answer.%K%P
然后…我将把我心中的答案，告诉她。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI should go back.\d%K%P
「回去吧…」%K%P
I began walking in the direction of the boarding house,\nunable to calm myself as my thoughts began to get\nincreasingly unsettling.%K%P
想象在我脑海中无数次翻滚，\n来来回回翻翻覆覆，\n最后我还是向着公寓，迈出了脚步。%K%P
The snow falling on East Hagimori had already piled up and\nwas starting to freeze over, making it difficult to find\ngood footing.%K%P
我已经踏足无数次的，\n仿佛要掩埋了东荻守的雪，\n开始渐渐地封冻了道路…%K%P
It all stimulated my anxiety and imagination, making me\nconsider the worst possible scenario.%K%P
我心中最初微微的不安，渐渐膨胀，\n渐渐地，浮现出了最坏的想象。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dPlease... be safe, Toko!\d%K%P
「求你了…一定要平安无事啊，都子！」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dLook, could you please stop killing me off in your\nimagination every time I'm a little late?\d%K%P
「我说啊，你能别摆出一副我快要完蛋了的样子好吗？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI can't help being worried! What else am I supposed to\ndo?!\n...Toko! Oh my god! Thank goodness you're alive!!\d%K%P
「因为我太担心了啊！\n………都子！太好了、太好了～！」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dH-Hey... Osamu!\d%K%P
「喂、喂喂…理君」%K%P
Unable to contain my emotions after having that disastrous\npossibility in my mind proven wrong, I embraced her with\nall my strength, attracting confused looks from passersby.%K%P
最坏的想象突然间消失殆尽，\n感激之余，我紧紧地抱住她，\n招来了旁人异样的目光。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dU-Um... Sorry I'm late. I just... couldn't decide on what\nI wanted to wear, that's all...\d%K%P
「那、那个，抱歉啊我来晚了。\n犹豫着该穿哪件衣服呢…不知该如何是好…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAll right, I see... thank goodness...\d%K%P
「嗯、嗯，太好了…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dYou're not even listening, are you...\d%K%P
「你听我说话啊喂…」%K%P
Toko bashfully pushed me away.%K%P
都子一边害羞地说着，\n一边扭扭捏捏地要挣脱我。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAh... I-I'm sorry...\d%K%P
「啊…抱、抱歉…」%K%P
